<center><table BORDER=0 CELLSPACING="10" CELLPADDING="0" WIDTH="100%" BGCOLOR="#FFFFFF">
<tr>
<td VALIGN=TOP WIDTH="33%" BGCOLOR="#FFFFFF" CELLSPACING="0" CELLPADDING="0" >
<font size="2" face="arial, helvetica">
<P><font size="4" face="arial, helvetica" COLOR="#990000"><b>History</b></font>
<p>
The Reckoners formed around 1993 during an AD&D game. The characters 
needed a name for their adventuring band and so the Reckoners we became due in large part 
to the warcry of Hilda the barbarian paladin, "Now Comes... The Reckoning!". (Hilda also 
devised the 'Circle of Doom'.)
<p>
The little group continued in play for several months before each went their seperate way. 
<p>
The Reckoners were reborn in 2000 when the same players assembled online to play Everquest 
on first the Tunare server then again on Bristlebane. 
<p>
Both times Mirabella Ebonheart established herself as our first guild leader. Asiah and 
Sharien SongRaven served as the first guild officers shortly followed by all their 
other numerous alts.
<p>
Guild membership was at first restricted to the original Reckoners only, (IE friends in real 
life) plus Andromada, the wife of one of the originals, but after grouping regularly with 
us for over 20 levels Vuurl joined the Reckoners. Bigburp Scuseme and Belgerard the mage did 
not but their alts did after they too spent several thousand hours with us. 
<p>
Asiah became the first Level 50 character, followed by Mirabella and Sharien. 
<p>
Currently the guild consists of the core group of 50+ characters: Mirabella, Asiah, Sharien, 
Jasada, Vuurl, Aleriel, and various younger groups of alts. The number, name and level of 
alts varies wildly. 
<p>
The Guild's main law is 'Need before Greed' when divvying loot.
<p>
<P><font size="4" face="arial, helvetica" COLOR="#990000"><b>Friends of the Reckoners</b></font>
